Third-party test vectors

The strict-Ed25519 conformance corpus file
priv/conformance/strict-ed25519/cases/taming/speccheck.json contains 12 Ed25519
test vectors imported byte for byte from ed25519-speccheck
(https://github.com/novifinancial/ed25519-speccheck, commit
65519336fda78a3d016e947df6d82848aca0c9da, file cases.json, SHA-256
08e47a36d9aead288664930505584f353fff113ab854f2800db1e4f5b3540450), which
accompanies "Taming the many EdDSAs" (Chalkias, Garillot, Nikolaenko,
SSR 2020; IACR ePrint 2020/1244). Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its
affiliates. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the upstream
repository carries no NOTICE file at that commit. The vectors are reproduced
unmodified; this project adds the base64url input encoding, expected verdicts,
and provenance fields around them. The same vectors also appear in the Go and
Rust SDK conformance snapshots under sdks/go/conformance/corpus-strict/ and
sdks/rust/conformance/corpus-strict/.
